  "description": "Reusable output profiles and explicit VDP assignments. Resolved once by the shared runtime catalogue.",
  "rules": {
    "capabilities": "Each key references a capability code; its array lists allowed value codes. Missing capabilities are unsupported.",
    "overrides": "Conditions match selected capability values. Matching overrides replace the named value lists; other lists remain unchanged. Replacements must be subsets of the profile lists.",
    "contexts": "Intersect profile values with capability and value contexts from the capability catalogue. Missing contexts impose no context restriction.",
    "runtime": "Runtime frame and renderer support may further restrict these lists.",
    "validation": "Reject unknown references, duplicate codes, conflicting matching overrides, and missing VDP assignments.",
    "crop_regions": "Rectangles use packed framebuffer pixels (x, y, width, height), not timing raster units. Sources name GC_VideoFrameDescriptor fields and must be read again when its revision changes. default_crop selects the existing presentation region; regions do not imply a user-selectable CROP capability. logical_window describes the LCD window within logical content coordinates.",
    "variants": "Default output profile per variant code; null means not implemented. Concrete machine options can reference a profile explicitly."
  },
